From ee38b8703e11e0fa1d4158272ea5614dcc4bb96f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] G2-EX step 2: held dims, clipped text, the aura as a kept
 rect list (exact)

- Verdict and result in layers. The verdict's whole-screen dim (15.8 ms of the GBA frame) and the failure's
  fade to black are clippable layers with keys that do not change: when something under them changes only
  that part is dimmed again, the rest of the screen keeps the dim it had. The holy heart + sparkles, the
  percentage and the caption (verdict) and the cloud / confetti, demon, title, line, figures strip and hint
  (result) are layers of their own in the order the one layer drew them; the title, line and strip are
  clippable too. (A failure's fade starts at shade level 0, which is black: kept, `fade_on`.)
- plat_clip honours plat_text and plat_text_outline (GBA: the glyph pixels inside the box; native already).
- The host's aura (two ellipses with the frame's hole left out: 5 ms of shape code and hole splitting on
  every pulse change, every third tick) is kept as the 40-76 rects it draws, one list per pulse (-2..2),
  and drawn again at the frame's place (plat_rect_run on the GBA's plain Mode 4 path, plat_rect otherwise).
  Lists live in the scene scratch (+3.8 KB there, none resident); a frame with rows off the screen is
  drawn as before. PS1 / Dreamcast (no holes) are unchanged.
- Tests: the ritual to the end of the result's fade for a failure and for a cast out (seeds are searched),
  stage on / off; the aura's list against the shape code; the clipped text primitives.
GBA full-ritual frames (1,382, deterministic portraits) identical to the base ROM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
